-- title:
--   Unit idèles at an admissible modulus are idelic norms
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ and $F$ be number fields with $F$ an extension of $E$ that is Galois over $E$, and let $\mathfrak f$ be an ideal of the ring of integers $\mathcal O_E$. Assume $\mathfrak f$ is an admissible modulus for the degree $n = [F:E]$, that is: $\mathfrak f \neq 0$, and for every finite place $v$ of $E$ for which the inertia subgroup in $\mathrm{Gal}(F/E)$ of the chosen prime `primeAbove E F v` of $\mathcal O_F$ above $v$ is nontrivial, one has $v^{e(v)} \mid \mathfrak f$ with exponent $e(v) = 1 + \sum_{p \mid n} (\mathrm{ord}_p(n) + 1)\, e(p\mathbb Z, v)$, the sum over the prime factors $p$ of $n$ and $e(p\mathbb Z, v)$ the ramification index of the ideal generated by $p$ at $v$. The conclusion is the inclusion of subgroups $\mathrm{unitIdeles}\ E\ \mathfrak f \le \mathrm{range}$ of the idelic norm attached to the canonical base change `genuineBaseChange E F`: every unit idèle $u \in (\mathbb A_E)^\times$ whose finite components all have valuation $1$, which satisfies $v(u_v - 1) \le \exp(-\mathrm{ord}_v \mathfrak f)$ at every finite $v$ dividing $\mathfrak f$, and which has positive component at the real place attached to each ring homomorphism $\tau : E \to \mathbb R$, is the image under `Units.map` of the adelic norm $\mathbb A_F \to \mathbb A_E$ (the algebra norm for the base-change map $\mathbb A_E \to \mathbb A_F$, with $\mathbb A_E \otimes_E F \cong \mathbb A_F$) of some unit idèle of $F$.
--
--   This is the idelic form of the classical statement that the group of norms from the idèles of $F$ contains the congruence subgroup of unit idèles of a sufficiently deep level, the level here being controlled purely by the degree $[F:E]$ rather than by class field theory. It is used in the construction of the idelic Artin map for $F/E$ (its kernel, surjectivity and expression as a product of Frobenius contributions) and in a counting statement about places whose local norm groups omit given elements.
